From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:46:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 521/521] [DS4.1] PDL: replay tests, a source check and two
 benchmarks

- test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_pdl: a reader that loads before its wait sees a
  slow producer's buffer unwritten inside a CUDA graph (the edges are
  programmatic) and a waiting reader never does; one decode layer's chain,
  every intermediate poisoned with NaN before each graph replay, gives its
  eager bits on every replay; TileKernels' switch is on.
- deepseek_v41_pdl_sources (pytest plugin): every kernel the DS4.1 kernel
  tests launch is checked in its CUDA source; chain kernels wait outside any
  block before naming a pointer parameter and trigger after, warp-specialized
  GEMMs have no PDL.
- deepseek_v41_pdl_chains: the layer chain at TP4's shapes (mHC entries with
  their MXFP8 casts, Q-A/KV on the attention entry's cast, q norm, Q-B,
  WO-A/WO-B, the shared expert on its own stream and the routed experts on the
  FFN entry's cast, combine; 20 kernels), built only on APIs that predate PDL.
- benchmark_deepseek_v41_pdl_chain: the chain in CUDA graphs, warm and
  L2-cold, with digests of every buffer, to compare builds with and without
  PDL.
- benchmark_deepseek_v41_pdl_mechanism: synthetic dependent kernels in four
  launch modes, a fork/join, and a replay of one traced decode layer.
